// project's OWN copy of the bytes, and the build-time resolver that keeps existing mods working.
//   useCatalogAsset()      a NEW pick: published only, the plan gate (canAsset create: sounds Saka+, visuals the top
//                          "All models" plan, free/Katara nothing), the licence tiers per plan and the proprietary
//                          clearance (resolveLibrarySlot of the catalog tools). The bytes are copied into the project
//                          (ProjectAssetSink -> CyrusProjectAsset in Nxeon); the owner's proprietary sounds are never
//                          copied raw: they stay a library render (layer `lib:<id>`, transformed at build time).
//                          The use is recorded (LibraryRecords.uses) so a takedown can mark its dependents.
//   resolveSlotForBuild()  what a build runs per library slot. A slot the project already holds a copy of is resolved
//                          from THAT copy, with NO plan gate and whatever the library status is now (keeping,
//                          installing, rebuilding and exporting are never gated; a removed asset keeps working in mods
